You guys used water-based paint? You're even more pathetic than I thought.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:18.950
See you later, losers.

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:20.110
Renamon?

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:30.000
Do growl, Mon. I can't afford oil.

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:40.010
It is everything I do always go so wrong

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:50.120
If only you could turn back at the deal, Mon. Please don't cry, Taka-Tamon. My arms are starting to run

00:18:50.440 --> 00:19:00.000
It'll be okay, Takato. Yeah, if first comes to worst we can always move Antarctica. Terrier, Mon.

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:01.310
Oh, he cooked.

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:03.310
Thanks, guys.

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.650
Sorry for the waterworks.

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:11.750
Huh?

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:15.500
It's not raining! Takato, look!

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.500
Sheesh, would you look already?

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:26.470
Pretty, whatever it is.

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:35.060
Those are the colors we should have painted Grom on.

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:38.800
Terriermon, we wanted him to blend in, not stick out like a sore thumb.

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:41.820
Well, he'd blend in fine if they were in the sky, wouldn't he?

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.310
Ooh, I gotta explain everything to you.

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:50.680
What's happening to Grom on, Henry?

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:53.240
Those flecks of light must be digital matter.

00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:55.520
And it looks like the rainbow is pulling them out of him.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:58.020
Or maybe the sun's just kind of drying him out.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.830
I don't know. It's weird.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.920
Not as weird as what I found between Grauman's toes when we were painting him.

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:03.820
True.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:05.120
Whoa!

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:11.130
Grauman! I mean, Gilman! Whoever you are, you're back to being Gilman!

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:14.770
Things are finally normal again.

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:17.190
Well, as normal as they get.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:22.080
So, we need to find a rainbow every time he wants to change back to Gilman?

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.800
How come no one wants to answer me today?

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:27.710
Does Takado need an instruction manual for Gilman, or what?

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:30.000
I wonder if these guys will ever figure out their partners.

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:32.760
Stay tuned to Digimon Digital Monsters.
